		(uuid "008cdd45-c4fe-4f15-b297-999aa82668c1")
	)
	(text "6. Feeder current sense: GPIO27/ADC1 = I x 50 mOhm (R23) x 50 (U8 INA181A2) = 2.5 V/A, REF = GND. Full scale ~1.3 A."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 231.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "05da6fa7-4260-4423-b7ee-6f40358afe92")
	)
	(text "FEEDER POWER MUX"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 431.8 139.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0cfe1b56-e821-4173-9f55-4d492ea03ccd")
	)
	(text "REV B ADDITIONS\n7. GPIO7 AUX_ACTIVE (TPS2116 ST: high = feeder powered from AUX USB-C), GPIO8 RECOVER_N (SW3).\n8. SWD probe J7: GPIO9 nRESET, GPIO10 SWCLK, GPIO11 SWDIO, GPIO23 SWO, GPIO22 VTREF detect (via R34 10k).\n9. Expansion J6: GPIO12/13 I2C (R32/R33 pull-ups not fitted), GPIO14, 15, 18-21, GPIO29/ADC3.\n10. GPIO28/ADC2 FDR_TX_SENSE via R30 100k. No DC load on FDR_TX (see note 3): firmware enables the\n    GPIO28 pull-down only while checking. FDR_TX still high after power cut = D-cell batteries still in.\n11. U9 priority mode: PR1 = VBUS_AUX x R28/(R27+R28) = 15k/62k vs 1.0 V ref -> feeder runs from aux above ~4.1 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 271.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3740e121-f74e-43a5-b837-62eb7d9ab6d2")
	)
	(text "FEEDER ALIVE SENSE"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 520.7 43.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "59a2e531-3c2a-4900-b01f-6b03dc64a40e")
	)
	(text "AUX FEEDER POWER  (USB-C, power only)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 431.8 43.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "60b51fd8-8a40-49f8-9044-9827ca295ea5")
	)
	(text "PLAF103 RECOVERY BOARD - NOTES\n1. Remove the feeder's D-cell batteries before recovery: cutting USB power will not reset the chip otherwise.\n2. All control lines default OFF via pulls: feeder unpowered (R10), strap released (R15), UART buffers disabled (R17/R18).\n3. No pull-up or pull-down on FDR_TX / FDR_RX: a pull-up would back-power an unpowered feeder,\n   and a pull-down could act as an unintended boot strap (feeder TX low at power-on = ROM download mode).\n4. J2 pin order matches feeder CON5: 1 = RX (square pad), 2 = TX, 3 = GND (next to screw).\n5. RP2040 GPIO: 0 ADP_TXD, 1 ADP_RXD, 2 FDR_PWR_EN (K1), 3 FDR_PWR_FLT_N, 4 STRAP_EN (K2),\n   5 UART_TX_OE_N (K3), 6 UART_RX_OE_N (K4), 16 LED_STATUS, 17 LED_UART, 26/ADC0 VBUS_FDR_SENSE (x0.6)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 220.98 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "87d9e433-06f0-409d-92be-3031badc6c3f")
	)
	(text "SWD DEBUG PROBE  (ARM 10-pin, not fitted)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 490.22 187.96 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ab857de2-0d14-4dbc-b9e8-10ce4808d2ee")
	)
	(text "REV C ADDITIONS\n12. Board ID straps: GPIO24 tied to GND, GPIO25 open. Firmware reads both with internal pull-ups enabled:\n    rev B = 11 (both open), rev C = 01. Change the copper straps on each new revision.\n13. Test jig (top side): TP1 SWCLK, TP2 SWDIO, TP3 GND, TP4 RUN, TP5 QSPI_SS (hold low at reset = BOOTSEL),\n    plus the bare J6 holes for +3V3 (pin 1), VBUS_IN (pin 2) and GND.\n14. Feeder UART ESD is U7 (USBLC6-2SC6) on FDR_RX / FDR_TX. Back silkscreen carries the REV C date code."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 287.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e912686d-6365-440b-8d2e-17eef8337c67")
	)
